 "rulebook": "WDBF Cloth Dodgeball Rules 2026 (World Dodgeball Federation): rule 1.1 (the playing court 18 m x 9 m), 1.3 (lines 5 cm wide, drawn inside the court; the centre line; the neutral zone lines 7 m from the back lines), 1.4 (fair territory, neutral zone), 2.1-2.3 (five balls of textured no-sting cloth over foam over a butyl bladder, 17.78 cm across, 110-125 mbar), 15.1 (a live player is out when hit by a live ball on any part of the body or clothing), 16.2 and 16.6 (a thrown ball is live from the throw until it touches a surface or a dead object that is not a ball), 26.1-26.5 (out of bounds: touching a boundary line, a surface outside them, the opponents' fair territory or the neutral zone line next to it: out)",
 "deviations": [
  "Rule 16 (the throwers): the five throws come from five two-wheel ball machines (the shared machine block, one ball each) standing in the opponents' fair territory 3.0 m beyond the centre line, their exits 1.2 m high, each on a turret (a yaw and a pitch joint driven by torque-limited servos, 20.0 and 30.0 N m) whose controller points it, until its feed, at where you are now: your pelvis, at a height of 0.8 m, with the elevation that the ball's drag needs for that distance; it does not lead a moving target. Each throws at 14.0 m/s with no spin, the first fed at 2.0 s and the others 2.5 s apart: an opposing team cannot be simulated.",
  "Rules 20-22 (blocks and catches): you hold no ball, so you cannot block, and the robot cannot catch: any contact of a live ball with you is a hit (rule 15.1 counts every part, the head too).",
  "Rule 2: the rules give no mass for the ball; it is 0.13 kg here (an estimate from its construction), its bounce, drag and stiffness are estimates from its pressure and build (said in the module).",
  "The match is reduced to one player surviving five throws (rule 9: sets, players, the opening rush and the shot clock of rule 18 do not apply); you must stay on your feet, which the rules do not require."
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Dodge: five cloth dodgeballs are thrown at you by ball machines that aim at you; do not let a live ball touch you, stay inside your court and on your feet.",
  "rules": "You stand in your fair territory on a WDBF cloth dodgeball court (18.0 m x 9.0 m, lines 5 cm wide drawn inside it), 5 m behind the centre line, facing it (+x). Five ball machines stand in the opponents' half, 3.0 m beyond the centre line, 1.5 m apart across the court (at 0, -3, +3, -1.5 and +1.5 m from its middle, in the order they throw), each holding one dodgeball (17.78 cm, 0.13 kg, cloth over foam, in air). Each machine's exit is 1.2 m above the floor; its turret points it at where your pelvis is at that moment, at a height of 0.8 m, allowing for the ball's drag, until it is fed; it throws at 14.0 m/s. The first is fed at 2.0 s, the others 2.5 s apart. A thrown ball is live from the moment it leaves its machine until it touches the floor or anything that is not you or a ball; then it is dead. You fail if a live ball touches any part of you (rule 15.1); if any part of you touches a boundary line or the floor outside them, the opponents' neutral zone line (7.0 m from their back line) or anything beyond it (rule 26); if you fall (your pelvis lower than 0.35 m above the floor, or any part of you other than the feet on the floor); or after 15.5 s. A throw is dodged when its ball is dead, or 3.0 s after it left the machine, without having touched you; you succeed when all five are dodged. The machines' wheels turn at 15.9 m/s at their rims (the throw's speed comes from them).",
  "venue": "A wooden sports floor with the 18 m x 9 m court painted on it; you stand in the middle of your half, 5 m behind the centre line, facing the opponents' half (+x), where the five machines stand in a row 8 m in front of you, their heads at about head height, turning to follow you. The side lines are 4.5 m to your left and right, your back line 4 m behind you.",
  "difficulty": "A ball thrown at you reaches you about 0.75 s after it leaves the machine, aimed where you were: standing still is a hit; the G1 has to be moving when each ball is thrown and keep moving, within its court, with a walking policy that makes about 0.5 m/s, and turn its narrow side to the throws."
 },
